\item{p_bio_vio_last_year}{Identifies if a biosolids violation has occured in the last year.  Valid values are Y and N.}

\item{p_msgp_rpt_year}{The last year that a MSGP report was submitted for the permit.  Valid values are "NONE" and any year Greater or Eqal to 2014.}

\item{p_vio_last_year}{Identifies if a permit violation has occured in the last year.  Valid values are Y and N.}

\item{responseset}{Response Set Limiter. Enter a value to limit the number of records per page. Value cannot exceed 1,000.}

\item{callback}{JSONP Callback.  For use with JSONP and GEOJSONP output only.  Enter a name of the function in which to wrap the JSON response.}

\item{qcolumns}{Used to customize service output.  A list of comma-separated column IDs of output objects that will be returned in the service query object or download.  Use the metadata service endpoint for a complete list of Ids and definitions.}

\item{p_pretty_print}{Optional flag to request GeoJSON formatted results to be pretty printed.  Only provide a numeric value when the output needs to be human readable as pretty printing has a performance cost.}

\item{p_e90_count}{Number of E90 Exceedances.  Identifies water permits with a number of E90 (Effluient Exceedances) >= the value provided for the last number of years provided by the p_e90_years value.}

\item{p_e90_years}{Number of years for the p_e90_count search.  Identified the past number of years to be used for the p_e90_count search.}

\item{p_pctlowinc}{Percent Low Income filter. Enter a value to restrict results to facilities with a given percentage of low income population within a 3-mile radius.}

\item{p_psc}{EPA Effluent Guidelines Point Source Category.}

\item{tidy}{Return a tibble (typed from ECHO metadata: numbers, dates and text; codes and IDs stay text). FALSE returns the decoded response. Non-JSON output formats and GeoJSON are always returned as sent.}
}
\value{
A tibble of the matching rows, typed from ECHO metadata, with the query summary, query ID and query parameters in attributes (tidy = TRUE, the default for JSON output), or the decoded response (tidy = FALSE).
}
